// REJECTS: Unexpected token ','. Valid alternatives: [')']
//
// Inside the range form of a milestoning clause the optional tail is ordered:
//     BUS_FROM = x, BUS_THRU = y (, THRU_IS_INCLUSIVE = b)? (, INFINITY_DATE = d)?
// The inclusive flag must PRECEDE INFINITY_DATE. This writes them the other way round.
//
// Both are optional, both are `NAME = value`, and neither reads like it belongs in a
// sequence -- which is exactly why a rewrite parses the tail as a bag of named arguments
// and accepts either order. The positive fixture relational-milestoning.pure writes the
// legal order on two tables and would not catch the difference.
###Relational
Database fixture::neg::InfinityFirst
(
   Table T
   (
      milestoning
      (
         business(BUS_FROM = FROM_Z, BUS_THRU = THRU_Z, INFINITY_DATE = %9999-12-31T00:00:00.0000, THRU_IS_INCLUSIVE = true)
      )
      ID VARCHAR(32) PRIMARY KEY,
      FROM_Z DATE,
      THRU_Z DATE
   )
)
